        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "+5V ---[D3 PMEG3030EP]--- NET0041 (sheet m5-pantilt, page 1)"}
      ],
      "impact": "With the diode reversed, the +5V rail cannot feed the servo power rail; the servos would receive no supply voltage and the board would be non-functional in either PWM or serial mode.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most component values and the overall PWM/serial topology match the specification, but the servo-rail Schottky diode D3 appears drawn with reversed polarity (cathode toward +5V), which would prevent +5V from powering the servo rail; confidence is limited by the small diode symbol in the drawing."
}

